 74-W- 184 ORNL Resonance Evaluation Including Covariance         7437 1451
 (ORNL AUG 2014)                                                  7437 1451
                                                                  7437 1451
 L. Leal, M. Pigni, K. Guber, D. Wiarda, and G. Arbanas           7437 1451
                                                                  7437 1451
 W-184 resolved resonance parameter evaluation was done in the    7437 1451
energy range form 1e-5 eV to 10 keV with the SAMMY code[ref1].    7437 1451
Capture and transmission measurements for enriched W-184 and      7437 1451
natural tungsten were used in the evaluation. The measurements    7437 1451
were done at the Oak Ridge Linear Accelerator (ORELA)[ref2] and   7437 1451
at the Geel Linear Accelerator (GELINA), Belgium[ref3]. Neutron   7437 1451
transmission and capture data were measured in the energy range   7437 1451
from 20 eV to 10 keV.                                             7437 1451
 Thermal cross section[ref4] data available in the EXFOR library  7437 1451
were also used in the evaluation.                                 7437 1451
                                                                  7437 1451
 Resonance parameter covariance matrices were also obtained in    7437 1451
the SAMMY evaluation process in the energy region 1e-5 eV-10 keV. 7437 1451
The RML formalist (LRF=7) was used for the resonance parameters   7437 1451
and the compact formalism (LCOMP=2) for the covariance matrix.    7437 1451
  Thermal cross section and uncertainty calculated with SAMMY and 7437 1451
the PUFF codes are compared with the values listed in the ATLAS   7437 1451
of Neutron Resoances in the table below. Also shown is the        7437 1451
capture resonance integral, Coherent scattering length and the    7437 1451
effective radius R'.                                              7437 1451
                                                                  7437 1451
    Cross Section        ORNL (b)           Atlas (b)             7437 1451
    -------------        --------           ---------             7437 1451
       Total          8.98 +/- 0.12             -                 7437 1451
       Capt           1.63 +/- 0.13         1.70 +/-  0.10        7437 1451
       Scat           7.35 +/- 0.10         7.35 +/-  0.10        7437 1451
                                                                  7437 1451
 Capture Res. Int.   16.01 +/- 0.17        14.7  +/-  1.5         7437 1451
                                                                  7437 1451
        R'            7.62 fm               8.0  +/-  0.2  fm     7437 1451
                                                                  7437 1451
        b_coher       7.41 fm              7.55e +/-  0.06 fm     7437 1451
                                                                  7437 1451
                                                                  7437 1451
 Average cross section and related uncertainties calculated in    7437 1451
energy group 0.0253 eV - 0.3 eV are listed in the table below.    7437 1451
                                                                  7437 1451
            Cross Section                Average Value (b)        7437 1451
            -------------                -----------------        7437 1451
                Total                  8.89 +/- 0.12 (1.3%)       7437 1451
                Capt                   1.56 +/- 0.11 (7.0%)       7437 1451
                Scat                   7.33 +/- 0.11 (1.5%)       7437 1451
                                                                  7437 1451
